  "rules": [
    "a name: 1 to 32 of a-z 0-9 _, the first a letter, no __, not ending in _; lowercase only on chain",
    "a number of the first form (protocol versions 1 and 2, and held on after): the 4 to 10 digits after +0, the first 1-9",
    "a number of the fixed form (protocol version 3): a code of three equal digits, one of 000 111 222 333 444 555 666 777 888 999, then 7 digits: 10 digits on chain, written +0 777 123 4567; a block of version 1 or 2 takes the first form only, one of version 3 both; a new handle (a bid) only a name or a fixed number",
    "reserved names: saltix salt work admin support help official security wallet bank city governor treasury exchange faucet explorer system root null, and every name starting with saltix",
    "name prices in SALT by length 1..7, then 8 and longer: 100000 25000 5000 1000 250 100 50 10 (from version 3 the starting bid of a name's auction); mint_price and short are the price rule's, null and false for a form it does not mint (+0 000 ...)",
    "the starting bids of version 3's auction terms: a name's length price; a fixed number's by its tier, the count of its 10 digits that are the code's digit or the seven after the code alone: ten (all 10 one digit) 100000 SALT, nine (the code's digit 9 times) 20000, seven_without_code (the 7 after the code one other digit) 5000, eight (the code's digit 8 times) 3000, seven_with_code (the code's digit 7 times) 500, plain (every other) 20; the tiers are disjoint, and the first in that order whose rule a number meets is its tier; tier and start_price are null for a name or a number of the first form only",
    "number prices in SALT by digits 4..7, then 8 and longer: 10000 2000 500 100 20",
    "short handles (names of 1-4 characters, numbers of 4-5 digits) are minted with the secret of a commit taken 600 to 86400 slots before (versions 1 and 2; MintHandle is refused from version 3)",
    "auctions (version 3): BidHandle's value is the bid; a bid on a free handle opens the auction at its starting bid or more, ends = opened + 5 * E slots for an epoch of E slots (432000 on the main network: five days); a raise is at least bid + ceil(bid * 5 / 100) and not by the leader, and the beaten bid goes back; a bid taken at slot s sets ends = max(ends, s + max(1, floor(E / 24))) (3600 on the main network: an hour); the first beacon block with slot >= ends settles it (at most 1000 a block, the earliest end first): the leader holds the handle, the bid splits as a mint's price",
    "a holder's auction (version 3, 21-names §4b): AuctionHandle {handle, start, step_bp, duration, extension}, amount 0, by the handle's holder, of a handle bound to no app and not on auction (or on its own auction without a bid, whose terms and time it replaces); start >= 1 SALT (holder_min_start), step_bp 100..=5000, duration E..=30 * E slots, extension 0..=E; a listing ends; ends = opened + duration; the first bid is at least start, a later one at least bid + max(1, ceil(bid * step_bp / 10000)), never by the holder nor the leader; a bid taken at slot s sets ends = max(ends, s + extension); while on auction no ListHandle, TransferHandle, ReleaseHandle or BindHandle; the first beacon block with slot >= ends hands the handle to the leader as a sale (the holder's primary cleared, minted kept) and pays the holder the bid less the 5% royalty, which splits as a sale's; with no bid it expires and the handle stays; CancelAuction {handle} by the holder before the first bid and before the end",
    "commit hash = derive \"Saltix handle commit v1\" of borsh(handle) ‖ sender account id ‖ 32-byte secret",
    "borsh(Handle): tag 0 Name(String) or 1 Number(String); HandleKind: u8 0 name, 1 number",
    "registry calls (action tag 1 {call, amount}), paid in SALT: CommitHandle 23 {hash}, MintHandle 24 {handle, secret: Option<[u8;32]>}, TransferHandle 25 {handle, to}, SetPrimary 26 {handle}, ClearPrimary 27 {kind}, ReleaseHandle 28 {handle}, ListHandle 29 {handle, price: u64}, UnlistHandle 30 {handle}, BuyHandle 31 {handle}, BindHandle 35 {handle, slug: Option<String>} (24-app-studio §2: the holder points it at a live grain it owns, or clears it with none; a transfer, a sale or a release clears it, and so does retiring the grain), BidHandle 60 {handle} (version 3), AuctionHandle 61 {handle, start: u64, step_bp: u16, duration: u64, extension: u64} (version 3), CancelAuction 62 {handle} (version 3)",
    "a sale's royalty is 5% of the price, rounded down; 10% of a mint and of a royalty go to the future payments fund, the rest to the service treasury",
    "display: @name; a fixed number as +0, its code, 3 digits and 4 (+0 777 123 4567); another number as +0 then its digits in groups of four from the right"
  ],
